#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 1: Mapear las entradas clásicas a un problema cuántico {#step-1-map-"
"classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we illustrate QPE to recover the eigenphase of a known "
"single-qubit unitary. The unitary whose phase we want to estimate is the "
"single-qubit phase gate applied to the target qubit:\n"
msgstr ""
"En este tutorial, ilustramos la QPE para recuperar la fase propia de una "
"unitaria de un solo qubit conocida. La unitaria cuya fase queremos estimar "
"es la compuerta de fase de un solo qubit aplicada al qubit objetivo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\theta)=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[2pt]\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= e^{i\\theta\\,|1\\rangle\\!\\langle 1|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\theta)=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[2pt]\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= e^{i\\theta\\,|1\\rangle\\!\\langle 1|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We prepare its eigenstate $|\\psi\\rangle=|1\\rangle$. Because $|1\\rangle$ "
"is an eigenvector of $U(\\theta)$ with eigenvalue $e^{i\\theta}$, the "
"eigenphase to be estimated is:\n"
msgstr ""
"Preparamos su estado propio $|\\psi\\rangle=|1\\rangle$. Dado que "
"$|1\\rangle$ es un vector propio de $U(\\theta)$ con valor propio "
"$e^{i\\theta}$, la fase propia a estimar es:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\varphi = \\frac{\\theta}{2\\pi} \\pmod{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\varphi = \\frac{\\theta}{2\\pi} \\pmod{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We set $\\theta=\\tfrac{1}{6}\\cdot 2\\pi$, so the ground-truth phase is "
"$\\varphi=1/6$. The QPE circuit implements the controlled powers $U^{2^k}$ "
"by applying controlled phase rotations with angles $\\theta\\cdot2^k$, then "
"applies the inverse QFT to the counting register and measures it. The "
"resulting bitstrings concentrate around the binary representation of "
"$1/6$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Establecemos $\\theta=\\tfrac{1}{6}\\cdot 2\\pi$, por lo que la fase "
"verdadera es $\\varphi=1/6$. El circuito QPE implementa las potencias "
"controladas $U^{2^k}$ aplicando rotaciones de fase controladas con ángulos "
"$\\theta\\cdot2^k$, luego aplica la QFT inversa al registro de conteo y lo "
"mide. Las cadenas de bits resultantes se concentran alrededor de la "
"representación binaria de $1/6$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit uses $m$ counting qubits (to set the estimation precision) plus "
"one target qubit. We begin by defining the building blocks needed to "
"implement QPE: the Quantum Fourier Transform (QFT) and its inverse, utility "
"functions to map between decimal and binary fractions of the eigenphase, and"
" helpers to normalize raw counts into probabilities for comparing simulation"
" and hardware results.\n"
msgstr ""
"El circuito utiliza $m$ qubits de conteo (para establecer la precisión de la"
" estimación) más un qubit objetivo. Comenzamos definiendo los bloques de "
"construcción necesarios para implementar la QPE: la transformada de Fourier "
"cuántica (QFT) y su inversa, funciones utilitarias para mapear entre "
"fracciones decimales y binarias de la fase propia, y funciones auxiliares "
"para normalizar los conteos brutos en probabilidades para comparar los "
"resultados de simulación y hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 2: Optimizar el problema para la ejecución en hardware cuántico "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We build the QPE circuit by preparing the counting qubits in superposition, "
"applying controlled phase rotations to encode the target eigenphase, and "
"finishing with an inverse QFT before measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Construimos el circuito QPE preparando los qubits de conteo en "
"superposición, aplicando rotaciones de fase controladas para codificar la "
"fase propia objetivo y finalizando con una QFT inversa antes de la "
"medición.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 3: Ejecutar utilizando primitivas de Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-"
"qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We set the number of shots and qubits for the experiment, and encode the "
"target phase $\\varphi = 1/6$ using $m$ binary digits. With these "
"parameters, we build the QPE circuit that will be executed on simulation, "
"default hardware, and Fire Opal–enhanced backends.\n"
msgstr ""
"Establecemos el número de disparos y qubits para el experimento, y "
"codificamos la fase objetivo $\\varphi = 1/6$ utilizando $m$ dígitos "
"binarios. Con estos parámetros, construimos el circuito QPE que se ejecutará"
" en simulación, hardware predeterminado y backends mejorados con Fire "
"Opal.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run MPS simulation {#run-mps-simulation}"
msgstr "Ejecutar simulación MPS {#run-mps-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we generate a reference distribution using the `matrix_product_state`"
" simulator and convert the counts into normalized probabilities for later "
"comparison with hardware results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero, generamos una distribución de referencia utilizando el simulador "
"`matrix_product_state` y convertimos los conteos en probabilidades "
"normalizadas para una comparación posterior con los resultados de "
"hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware {#run-on-hardware}"
msgstr "Ejecutar en hardware {#run-on-hardware}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware with Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-opal}"
msgstr "Ejecutar en hardware con Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-opal}"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 4: Post-procesar y devolver el resultado en el formato clásico deseado "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/quantum-phase-"
"estimation-qctrl/extracted-outputs/593334d2-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Salida de la celda de código anterior](/docs/images/tutorials/quantum-"
"phase-estimation-qctrl/extracted-outputs/593334d2-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The simulation sets the baseline for the correct eigenphase. Default "
"hardware runs show noise that obscures this result, as noise spreads "
"probability across many incorrect bitstrings. With Q-CTRL Performance "
"Management the distribution becomes sharper and the correct outcome is "
"recovered, enabling reliable QPE at this scale.\n"
msgstr ""
"La simulación establece la línea base para la fase propia correcta. Las "
"ejecuciones de hardware predeterminadas muestran ruido que oscurece este "
"resultado, ya que el ruido distribuye la probabilidad entre muchas cadenas "
"de bits incorrectas. Con la gestión de rendimiento de Q-CTRL, la "
"distribución se vuelve más nítida y el resultado correcto se recupera, lo "
"que permite una QPE confiable a esta escala.\n"

